			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4435742">
									

<p>I like this. It started off simple but interesting enough that even without the resurrection of Sarah I would have up voted based on the test logs alone.</p>
<p>I do have a few (possibly nitpicky) concerns. I find it a little bit hard to understand exactly <em>why</em> the foundation kept Michael from using it. Sure, there may have been personal motivation, but there's no implication of him going against regulations in any way. If he was doing so in a controlled environment, I don't see why the foundation would have a problem. Other SCPs are used for personal gain of employees at times, and unless there was a clear danger at play (of which there is none here) the foundation is usually a-okay with it. If you are to add or rewrite part of this I would either remove their restrictions on him or write some reason in why the foundation would care.</p>
<p>Also, I don't quite understand that last blurb. Are they giving amnestics to Sarah or her parents? The blurb seems to imply that it's meant to stop her <em>parents</em> from forming attachments, which makes little sense if they were given to her.</p>
<p>Regardless, I enjoyed this article. +1</p>

							</div>

								
