<p>At the very least, I wonder if you might rethink this statement:</p>
<p>&quot;UPDATE: SCP-4469-A has begun to increase in intellect and intelligence. Subject's mental age is theorized to reach her normal age by late September of 2033.&quot;</p>
<p>It's not particularly clinical in tone, for example what is a &quot;normal age&quot; in this context? Also, how could the Foundation possible quantify exactly what someone's &quot;mental age&quot; is, much less with such precision that they can predict an exact month at which it would presumably &quot;catch up&quot; to her biological age?</p>
<p>I think you can just drop that line completely. If you really want to keep it for some reason, perhaps change it to something like &quot;UPDATE: SCP-4469-A has exhibited accelerated emotional development and mental maturation since containment, more consistent with her apparent biological age than a teenage individual. Observations are ongoing.&quot;</p>

